//RS // Shared helpers for every `tests/dev*.rs` target (`include!`d, never a module
//RS // of its own — see tests/cli_parts and tests/corelib_parts for the same shape).
//RS //
//RS // #2020: `tests/dev.rs` used to be one 11.8k-line binary carrying all 166 of
//RS // these tests. Its whole-corpus batteries run serially against one
//RS // `dev_diff_lock`, so the binary needed longer than the 900s suite guard and
//RS // aborted with about 30 of its own declared tests never started — every pass/fail
//RS // number it ever printed was a partial measurement. The guard is right and the
//RS // budget is not raisable, so the cost is split across targets instead: one routine
//RS // target plus one
//RS // per whole-corpus battery. This file is the single copy of everything they
//RS // share, so the split cannot fork a helper into two versions (AGENTS.md I8).
