//RS /// #2017: run one tier of one example in its own child, with the answers the
//RS /// golden was recorded with on its own fd 0.
//RS ///
//RS /// The choice, recorded here because the card asks for it: a SUBPROCESS, not an
//RS /// injected reader. The in-process entry points (`dev_iteration`,
//RS /// `CraneliftBackend::run`) read the test binary's own fd 0, which every thread
//RS /// of a parallel suite shares, so there is nothing per-run to redirect there;
//RS /// and an injected reader would exercise an input path no user has, which is
//RS /// exactly the sort of harness-only seam an I9 differential is supposed to
//RS /// catch rather than contain. A child reads stdin the way a user's program
//RS /// does, through the same CLI entry point.
//RS ///
//RS /// `trace` asks the run for `--trace-tiers`, which puts the tier attribution on
//RS /// stderr and therefore makes stderr unusable as a byte comparison — so a
//RS /// caller that needs both takes two runs: one to learn WHICH tier answered, one
